[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The board's one data source is the resident scribe daemon

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-SDOC-BOARD-READS-THE-SCRIBE-DAEMON
TITLE: The board's one data source is the resident scribe daemon
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: The daemon grows a typed query interface that supersedes the JSON export as the read path, or the board stops being read-only.
STATEMENT: >>>
The board's one data source is the resident scribe daemon. The server asks
workspace.describe for the held generation, calls workspace.export when it
moved, adapts the exported JSON, and caches the adapted payloads keyed by
generation; it never imports strictdoc, never loads a second graph, and never
runs an exporter subprocess. When no daemon answers, API requests refuse with
the client's own remedy (HTTP 503 naming devenv up scribe) and the page renders
that refusal with a retry; there is deliberately no fallback load.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One loaded graph per worktree already exists, reconciles itself on every read,
and exports in about 0.3 s. Both spikes duplicated it: the board hydrated its
own in-process StrictDoc workspace (3.4 s cold) beside the daemon's, and the
explorer paid a 2.2 s strictdoc export subprocess on every page load. The
export lands under output/, which the daemon's freshness sweep and the UID walk
both skip, so serving never dirties what it serves.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Written 2026-09-01 for the merge. It replaces the codex spike's data-plane
decisions (DEC-SDOC-BOARD-SERVER-OWNS-SNAPSHOT, DEC-SDOC-BOARD-COHOST-ADAPTERS,
DEC-SDOC-BOARD-LOCAL-RPC, DEC-SDOC-PERSPECTIVE-EXPORT-BOUNDARY): the spike's
private workspace, its Unix-socket RPC and its per-request exporter are all
dropped in favour of the daemon this branch already runs. Those nodes never
landed on this branch, so there are no Superseded_By edges to write -- the
provenance lives here instead.
<<<
